# Rimvio Dual Experience (locked)

**Canonical:** `docs/RIMVIO_DUAL_EXPERIENCE.md` · ADR-058

> **두 개의 Cursor** — User는 Globe에서 *무엇을 하고 싶은지*, Dev는 Hub Dev Workspace에서 *Agent가 쓸 Platform·Capability*를 만든다. 연결점: **Hub Publish → Capability Registry → Agent Discovery**.

## Stack

```text
USER:  Utterance → Intent → Task Graph → Capability Registry → Execute → Prepare → Commit
DEV:   Utterance → AI Plan → Platform Graph Patch → Sandbox → Preview → Hub Publish → Registry
```

## Do

- Agent discovers **capabilities** (`discover-capabilities`, `capability-index`) — not platform home URLs
- Dev work in `components/hub/deploy/` — NL-first; **배포해** runs `hub-deploy-runtime` loop
- Publish registers manifest → registry — only then Agent may invoke
- User UI: work log (“호텔 검색 ✓”) — hide Capability/Platform/Manifest nouns (L1)
- Side effects: Prepare until human Commit (booking · payment)
- Extend Platform OS via `lib/platform-sdk/` — do not reinvent permission/registry/runtime

## Don't

- Direct vendor API from Globe chat bypassing registry
- Hub as form-only admin dashboard without AI execute loop
- Auto Commit on booking/payment from agent
- Parallel discovery stores beside capability-index + workspace
- Teach Dev with folder-tree IA as primary — Platform **graph** is SSOT

## Reference vertical

OsakaStay (hotel.search → booking.prepare → payment.commit) is the **e2e acceptance story** for both experiences — implement as published platform, not Globe-only hacks.

## PR reject

- User-facing “Capability”“Manifest” in hero/empty states
- Agent tool invoke before `planObjectDiscovery` / capability discovery on search flows
- Publish path that skips registry registration
- Dev feature that bypasses manifest validation or sandbox test gate
